  "name": "abyss-dive",
  "vibe": "Ink-teal water (#061c26) with bioluminescent cyan (#35d0d6), a coral orange and a sand cream, set in wide Krona One. Uniquely, the world never cuts away — it runs under every single beat including the closer. Hollow cyan bubbles wobble upward the full height, a coral jellyfish drifts on a slow lissajous with a scalloped hem that breathes and three tentacles that undulate, an anglerfish orb pulses on its sand filament, and a depth ladder ticks 100m to 500m down the right edge. Rotation is near zero at 0.4°; the drift is vertical, the title easing is a drowse, and cards, tiles and stat numbers all glow. Mechanics: a sonar terminal typewriter, a dive-log feed, a hull ring and side-docked surface messages. Best for marine and environmental work, research and documentary series.",
